---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Does Can I Vibecode It? track you?"
  description="No third-party analytics, ad pixels, accounts, or cross-site tracking."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="narrow-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY / PLAIN ENGLISH</p>
      <h1>Does this site track you?</h1>
      <p>No ad pixels. No cross-site profiles. No dark patterns.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <article class="prose narrow-shell">
    <h2>What gets stored?</h2>
    <p>
      If you vote, the server stores a one-way salted hash of your IP address
      for 24-hour rate limiting. The raw address is not stored in the
      application database. If you join the waitlist, we store the email you
      submit and the same salted network hash for abuse prevention.
    </p>
    <h2>What runs in your browser?</h2>
    <p>
      Vanilla JavaScript powers search, filters, copy buttons, motion, and the
      theme switch. Your chosen theme is remembered in local storage. There are
      no third-party analytics scripts, advertising tags, or social widgets.
    </p>
    <h2>Can I remove my email?</h2>
    <p>
      Yes. Open an issue in the public repository with a safe contact method;
      do not post the address publicly. We will verify ownership and remove it.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
